18 The command line
*******************

‘esploro [FOLDER]’
     FOLDER (by default the one you're in) in the Esploro window
     on your workspace, or a new one there.
‘esploro --new [FOLDER]’
     A new Esploro window.
‘esploro FILE’
     The file's folder, with FILE selected.
‘esploro --where [PATH...]’
     Which windows have PATH open, or every file that's open.
‘esploro reveal’
     The file behind the window you're in, selected in its
     folder.
‘esploro recipe list’
‘esploro recipe last’
‘esploro recipe save NAME’
‘esploro recipe forget NAME’
‘esploro recipe run NAME|last FILE...’
     Recipes (*note Recipes::): the last change, or one kept by
     name, done again on FILE....  A rename or a sorting goes to
     Esploro for your review; with ‘--plan’ (‘run --plan’) it
     only answers with the plan's file.
‘esploro recipe add NAME RECIPE’
     Keep RECIPE, an s-expression such as ‘(:rename-by "IMG_*"
     "Pic #n")’, by name.
‘esploro rename-by [--plan] FROM TO FILE...’
‘esploro sort-by-kind [--plan] FILE...’
     Rename by a pattern, or sort into folders by kind (*note
     Recipes::): the plan goes to Esploro for your review.
‘esploro query [--lines] WORDS [FOLDER]’
     The files below FOLDER that WORDS describe (*note
     Searches::), one a line with ‘--lines’.
‘esploro search list’
‘esploro search save NAME WORDS [FOLDER]’
‘esploro search forget NAME’
‘esploro search run [--lines] NAME’
     Searches kept by name.
‘esploro learn PROPOSED APPLIED’
     What APPLIED (your plan) changed in PROPOSED (an agent's),
     as rules in words.
‘esploro learn --add RULE’
     RULE into ‘~/.config/esploro/sorting.md’, under its learnt
     rules.
‘esploro habits [--new]’
     What you keep doing, each with a rule, a recipe and a
     search; ‘--new’, only those not told of before.
‘esploro habits --dismiss KEY’
     That one, never offered again.
‘esploro archive open PATH’
‘esploro archive close MOUNTPOINT’
‘esploro archive list’
     An archive opened read-only like a folder (*note
     Archives::), closed, and the ones open.
‘esploro workspaces’
     StumpWM's workspaces, each with the project its windows are
     about.
‘esploro open-on N PATH...’
     Goes to workspace N and opens PATH there.
‘esploro selection [--sexp]’
     The files selected in Esploro, or dired, used last, one a
     line; ‘--sexp’ gives ‘(:selection FOLDER (FILE...))’.
‘esploro propose FILE [WHY]’
     A plan for you to review in Esploro (what an agent's
     proposal runs).
‘esploro --dbus’
     Makes the running Emacs answer
     ‘org.freedesktop.FileManager1’, the file manager's name on
     D-Bus that browsers call for "Show in folder".  A D-Bus
     service file naming it starts it the first time it's asked
     (Vikix puts one in ‘~/.local/share/dbus-1/services’).

   What the window uses (each answers with one s-expression):

‘esploro apply [FILE]’
     Applies the plan in FILE, or on standard input: one step a
     line, ‘(:copy "/from" "/to")’, ‘(:move ...)’, ‘(:rename
     "/path" "new name")’, ‘(:mkdir "/path")’, ‘(:trash
     "/path")’.  Anything else is refused.
‘esploro undo’
     Undoes the last applied plan.
‘esploro where FOLDER’
     The files in FOLDER a window has open.
‘esploro open PATH’
     Goes to the window that has PATH, or opens it.
‘esploro project [PATH]’
     PATH's project, and the windows that have something in it.
‘esploro focus ID’
     Goes to the window ID (StumpWM's).
‘esploro thumbnails [--size N] PATH...’
     Small PNGs of pictures, PDFs and videos for the list, each
     made once.
‘esploro preview PATH’
     A PNG of PATH (a picture, a PDF or a video), made once and
     kept.
‘esploro trash-list’
‘esploro restore NAME...’
‘esploro empty-trash’
     The Trash.


